===Etymology===
From Gay's Latin alphabet {{m|sh|A}}, from {{der|mul|cs|-}} alphabet {{m|cs|A}}, from the {{der|mul|ett|-}} letter {{m|ett|𐌀}}, from the {{der|mul|grc|-}} letter {{m|grc|Α||alpha}}, derived from the {{der|mul|phn|-}} letter {{m|phn|𐤀||[[aleph]]}}, from the {{der|mul|egy|-}} hieroglyph {{m|egy|𓃾}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{qualifier|phoneme|tonal variety}}: {{IPA|sl|/áː/|/àː/|/ʌ́/|/a/|[â]|[ǎ]}}
* {{qualifier|phoneme|non-tonal variety}}: {{sl-IPA|aː|a}}
* {{qualifier|letter name}}: {{sl-IPA|ā}}
* {{audio|sl|Sl-nt-á.ogg|q=letter name, non-tonal}}
* {{rhymes|sl|aː}}
* {{homophones|sl|a}}

===Letter===
{{head|sl|letters|upper case||lower case|a}}

# {{Latn-def|sl|letter|1}}
# {{Latn-def|sl|alphabet name=Resian|letter|1}}
# {{Latn-def|sl|alphabet name=Natisone Valley dialect|letter|1}}

===Noun===
{{sl-noun|Ā|m-in}}

# {{ng|The name of the [[Appendix:Latin script|Latin script]] letter '''''[[A]]''''' / '''''a'''''.}}

====Inflection====
* Overall more common
{{sl-decl-noun-m|Ā|Ā-j}}

* More common when with a definite adjective
{{sl-decl-noun-table2|Ā|Ā|Ā|Ā|Ā|Ā|Ā|Ā|Ā|Ā|Ā|Ā|Ā|Ā|Ā|Ā|Ā|Ā|title=Masculine inan., no endings}}

====Derived terms====
{{col4|sl|od A do Ž|ena A|od A do B|Á|Ä}}

===See also===
{{list:Latin script letters/sl/simple}}
* {{l|sl|Ä}}
* {{l|sl|A|Á}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:sl:Fran}}

-------- end text --------
Page 2 a: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=sl}}

===Etymology 1===
From [[w:Gaj's Latin alphabet|Gaj's Latin alphabet]] {{m|sh|a}}, from {{der|sl|cs|-}} alphabet {{m|cs|a}}, modification of capital {{m|mul|A}}, itself derived from the {{der|sl|ett|-}} letter {{m|ett|𐌀}}, from the {{der|sl|grc|-}} letter {{m|grc|Α||alpha}}, derived from the {{der|sl|phn|-}} letter {{m|phn|𐤀||aleph}}, from the {{der|sl|egy|-}} hieroglyph {{m|egy|𓃾}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{q|phoneme|tonal variety}}: {{IPA|sl|/áː/|/àː/|/ʌ́/|/a/|[â]|[ǎ]}}
* {{q|phoneme|non-tonal variety}}: {{IPA|sl|/aː/|/a/}} <!--{{sl-IPA|aː|a}}-->
* {{q|letter name}}: {{IPA|sl|/àː/|/áː/}} <!--{{sl-IPA|ā}}-->
* {{audio|sl|Sl-nt-á.ogg|q=letter name, non-tonal}}
* {{rhymes|sl|aː}}
* {{homophones|sl|a}}

====Letter====
{{head|sl|letter|lower case||upper case|A}}

# {{Latn-def|sl|letter|1}}
# {{Latn-def|sl|letter|1|alphabet name=Resian}}
# {{Latn-def|sl|letter|1|alphabet name=Natisone Valley dialect}}

====Symbol====
{{head|sl|symbol}}

# {{q|[[wikipedia:Slovene_national_phonetic_transcription|SNPT]]}} ''[[phonetic|Phonetic]] [[transcription]] of sound'' [{{IPAlink|a|ä}}].

====Noun====
{{head|sl|noun|head=ā|g=m-in}}

# {{n-g|The name of the [[Appendix:Latin script|Latin script]] letter '''''[[A]]''''' / '''''a'''''.}}
# {{n-g|The name of the [[phoneme]]s ''/{{IPAlink|a}}, {{IPAlink|aː}}, {{IPAlink|ʌ}}/''.}}

=====Inflection=====
* Overall more common
{{sl-decl-noun-m|ā|ā-j}}

* More common when with a definite adjective
{{sl-decl-noun-table2|ā|ā|ā|ā|ā|ā|ā|ā|ā|ā|ā|ā|ā|ā|ā|ā|ā|ā|title=Masculine inan., no endings}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l-self|sl|à}}, {{l-self|sl|á}}, {{l-self|sl|ā}}, {{l-self|sl|ȁ}}, {{l-self|sl|ȃ}}
* {{l|sl|ã}}, {{l|sl|ȧ}}, {{l|sl|ä}}, {{l|sl|å}}, {{l|sl|ḁ}}, {{l|sl|ą}}
* {{l|sl|če si rekel a, reci tudi b}}
* {{l|sl|ena a}}
* {{l|sl|od a do ž}}

===Etymology 2===
Attested since the 18th century. Probably of onomatopoeic origin. Compare {{cog|sh|a}}, {{cog|ru|а}}, {{cog|lt|o|õ}}, {{cog|la|o|ō}} and {{cog|grc|ὦ}}. These could all derive from Proto-Indo-European interjection {{m|ine-pro||*ō|oh, ah}}, but each form in individual languages could easily be an independent, expressive formation.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|sl|/àː/|/áː/|/á/}} <!--{{sl-IPA|ā|ȁ}}-->
* {{audio|sl|Sl-nt-á.ogg|q=non-tonal, long}}
* {{audio|sl|Sl-nt-à.ogg|q=non-tonal, short}}

* {{rhymes|sl|aː}}
* {{homophones|sl|A|a}}

====Interjection====
{{head|sl|interjections}} <!-- {{sl-interjection|-}} -->

# [[oh]]
# ''Used at the end of a sentence for confirmation, similarly to'' 'didn't I' ''in English.''
#: {{ux|inline=1|sl|Tega nisi pričakoval, '''a'''?|You did not expect this, '''did you'''?}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|sl|ah}}
* {{l|sl|e}}
* {{l|sl|eh}}
* {{l|sl|o}}
* {{l|sl|oh}}
* {{l|sl|uh}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|sl|sla-pro|*a}}, from {{inh|sl|ine-pro|*ō̃t}}, which is [[ablative]] form of {{inh|sl|ine-pro|*e-}} 'this'. Cognates with {{cog|sh|a}}, {{cog|ru|а}} and {{cog|cs|a}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|sl|/a/}} <!--{{sl-IPA|a}}-->

====Conjunction====
{{head|sl|conjunctions}} <!-- {{sl-con|-}} -->

# [[but]]
#: {{synonyms|sl|in|pa|toda|vendar}}

====Particle====
{{head|sl|particles}} <!-- {{sl-part|-}} -->

# {{form of|sl|contracted form|ali}}, particle used to form a yes- no question.
#: {{synonyms|sl|kaj|ali}}

