Page 4 À: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Letter {{l|sl|A}} with grave ({{l|sl|̀|◌̀}}) to signify long stressed vowel.

===Pronunciation===
* {{qualifier|sound}}: {{IPA|sl|/á/}}
* {{qualifier|letter name}}: {{sl-IPA|krátki ā}} ({{l|sl|kratki a}})
* {{rhymes|sl|aː}}

===Letter===
{{sl-letter|upper=À|lower=à}}

# ''Additional letter, used to denote the short stress on {{l|sl|A}}.''

====Usage notes====
Use of upper case letter is pretty limited as it can only appear on the last syllable. Therefore, upper case letter can appear in monosyllabic words and if writing in [[all caps]].

===See also===
* {{l|sl|A}}
* {{l|sl|Ä}}
* {{l|sl|Á}}
* {{l|sl|Ă}}

-------- end text --------
Page 5 á: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Letter {{l|sl|a}} with acute ({{l|sl||◌́}}) to signify long vowel.

====Pronunciation====
* {{qualifier|phoneme}}: {{IPA|sl|/áː/|/àː/}}
* {{qualifier|letter name|}}: {{sl-IPA|dȏłgi ā}}, {{l|sl|dolgi a}}
* {{rhymes|sl|aː}}

====Letter====
{{head|sl|letters|lower case||upper case|Á}}

# ''Additional letter, used in some words to denote the long stress on a.''

====Symbol====
{{head|sl|symbols}}

# {{qualifier|[[wikipedia:Slovene_national_phonetic_transcription|non-tonal SNPT]]}} ''[[phonetic|Phonetic]] [[transcription]] of sound ''[{{IPAlink|aː|ä}}].

===Etymology 2===
Letter {{l|sl|a}} with acute ({{l|sl||◌́}}) to signify long low-pitched vowel.

====Pronunciation====
* {{qualifier|phoneme}}: {{IPA|sl|/àː/|[ǎː]}}
* {{qualifier|letter name|tonal transcription}}: {{sl-IPA|akutȋrani ā}}, {{l|sl|akutirani a}}
* {{rhymes|sl|aː}}

====Symbol====
{{head|sl|symbols}}

# {{qualifier|[[wikipedia:Slovene_national_phonetic_transcription|tonal SNPT]]}} ''[[phonetic|Phonetic]] [[transcription]] of sound ''[{{IPAlink|àː|ä}}].

=====Usage notes=====
Symbol is sometimes used as a letter to denote pitch in a word, but that is mostly limited to foreign or specialized dictionaries.

===Etymology 3===
Letter {{l|sl|a}} with acute ({{l|sl||◌́}}) to signify short vowel.

====Pronunciation====
* {{qualifier|Natisone Valley dialect|phoneme}}: {{IPA|sl|/ˈa/}}

====Letter====
{{head|sl|letters|lower case||usually not in upper case}}

# {{qualifier|[[wikipedia:Natisone_Valley_dialect|Natisone Valley dialect]]}} ''Additional letter, used in some words to denote the short stress on a.''

===Etymology 4===
Letter {{l|sl|a}} with acute {{l|sl|´}} to signify stress.

====Pronunciation====
* {{qualifier|Resian|sound}}: {{IPA|sl|/a/}}

====Letter====
{{head|sl|letters|lower case||upper case|Á}}

# {{qualifier|[[wikipedia:Resian_dialect|Resian]]}} ''Additional letter, used in some words to denote the stress on a.''

===See also===
* {{l|sl|a}}
* {{l|sl|a|à}}
* {{l|sl|a|ȃ}}
* {{l|sl|a|ā}}
* {{l|sl|a|ȁ}}

