===Etymology 1===
{{der+|sl|de|Ä}}, with its corresponding pronunciation, which is still used by some speakers, however, the majority of speakers have vernacularized the pronunciation to a long close-mid vowel regardless of the initial pronunciation.

====Pronunciation====
* {{q|phoneme}}: {{IPA|sl|/éː/|/èː/|[ɛ́ː]}}
* {{q|letter name|common}}: {{sl-IPA|preglašéni ā}} ({{l|sl|preglašeni a}})
* {{q|letter name|educated}}: {{sl-IPA|ē}}
* {{rhymes|sl|ɛː}}
* {{homophones|sl|e}}

====Letter====
{{head|sl|letter|upper case||lower case|ä}}

# ''Additional letter in Slovene common mostly in loanwords from [[German]].''

