Page 235 b: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=sl}}

===Etymology===
From Gay's Latin alphabet {{m|sh|b}}, from {{der|mul|cs|-}} alphabet {{m|cs|b}}, from Latin {{m|la|b}}, modification of capital letter {{m|mul|B}} by dropping its upper loop, which is derived from the {{der|mul|ett|-}} letter {{m|ett|𐌁||be}}, from the {{der|mul|grc|-}} letter {{m|grc|Β||beta}}, derived from the {{der|mul|phn|-}} letter {{m|phn|𐤁||[[bet]]}}, from the {{der|mul|egy|-}} hieroglyph {{m|egy|𓉐}}. Pronunciation as {{IPA|sl|/bə/}} is initial Slovene (phoneme plus a fill vowel) and the second pronunciation is probably taken from {{der|sl|de|B}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{qualifier|phoneme}}: {{IPA|sl|/b/|[p]|[b̪]}}
* {{qualifier|letter name}}: {{sl-IPA|bə̏|bẹ̄}}
* {{audio|sl|Sl-nt-bə.ogg|q=letter name, non-tonal}}
* {{rhymes|sl|ə|eː}}

===Letter===
{{sl-letter|upper=B|lower=b}}

# {{Latn-def|sl|letter|2}}
# {{Latn-def|sl|letter|3|alphabet name=Resian}}
# {{Latn-def|sl|letter|2|alphabet name=Natisone Valley dialect}}

===Symbol===
{{head|sl|symbols}}

# {{qualifier|[[wikipedia:Slovene_national_phonetic_transcription|SNPT]]}} ''[[phonetic|Phonetic]] [[transcription]] of sound'' [{{IPAlink|b|b}}].

===Noun===
{{sl-noun|b|m-in}}

# {{n-g|The name of the [[Appendix:Latin script|Latin script]] letter '''''[[B]]''''' / '''''[[b]]'''''.}}
# {{lb|sl|linguistics}} {{n-g|The name of the [[phoneme]] ''/{{IPAlink|b}}/''.}}

====Inflection====
* Overall more common
{{sl-decl-noun-m|b|b-j}}

* More common when with a definite adjective
{{sl-decl-noun-table2|b|b|b|b|b|b|b|b|b|b|b|b|b|b|b|b|b|b|title=Masculine inan., no endings}}

===Derived terms===
{{col4|sl|če si rekel a, reci tudi b|ƀ}}

===See also===
{{list:Latin script letters/sl}}
