Page 579 c: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|sl|ƞ}} ([[wikipedia:Metelko_alphabet|Metelko alphabet]])
* {{l|sl|z}} ([[wikipedia:Bohorič_alphabet|Bohorič alphabet]])

===Etymology===
From Gaj's Latin alphabet {{m|sh|c}}, from Czech alphabet {{m|cs|c}}, from latin {{m|la|c}}, which is a modification of upper case letter {{m|mul|C}}, from Etruscan {{m|ett|𐌂}}, from Ancient Greek {{m|grc|Γ||Gamma}}, from Phoenician {{m|phn|𐤂||gimel}}. Pronunciation as {{IPA|sl|/cə/}} is initial Slovene (phoneme plus a fill vowel) and the second pronunciation is probably taken from {{der|sl|de|c}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{qualifier|phoneme}}: {{IPA|sl|/t͡s/|[d͡z]}}
* {{qualifier|letter name}}: {{sl-IPA|cə̏|cẹ̄}}
* {{audio|sl|Sl-nt-c.ogg|q=letter name, non-tonal}}
* {{rhymes|sl|ə|eː}}

===Letter===
{{sl-letter|upper=C|lower=c}}

# {{Latn-def|sl|letter|3}}
# {{Latn-def|sl|letter|4|alphabet name=Resian}}
# {{Latn-def|sl|letter|3|alphabet name=Natisone Valley dialect}}

===Symbol===
{{head|sl|symbols}}

# {{qualifier|[[wikipedia:Slovene_national_phonetic_transcription|SNPT]]}} ''[[phonetic|Phonetic]] [[transcription]] of sound'' [{{IPAlink|t͡s}}].

===Noun===
{{sl-noun|c|m-in}}

# {{n-g|The name of the [[Appendix:Latin script|Latin script]] letter '''''[[C]]''''' / '''''[[c]]'''''.}}
# {{lb|sl|linguistics}} {{n-g|The name of the [[phoneme]] ''/{{IPAlink|t͡s}}/''.}}

====Inflection====
* Overall more common
{{sl-decl-noun-m|c|c-j}}

* More common when with a definite adjective
{{sl-decl-noun-table2|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|title=Masculine inan., no endings}}

====Derived terms====
{{col4|sl|č|ć|ċ}}

