* {{l|sl|ɥ}} {{q|Metelko alphabet|Danjko alphabet}}
* {{l|sl|zh}} {{q|Bohorič alphabet}}

===Etymology===
From Gaj's Latin alphabet {{m|sh|ć}}, from Czech alphabet {{m|cs|č}}, from Latin {{m|la|c}}, a modification of uppercase letter {{m|mul|C}}, from Etruscan {{m|ett|𐌂}}, from Ancient Greek {{m|grc|Γ||Gamma}}, from Phoenician {{m|phn|𐤂||gimel}}. Pronunciation as {{IPA|sl|/t͡ʃə/}} is initial Slovene (phoneme plus a fill vowel) and the second pronunciation is probably by analogy of {{der|sl|de|C}} from German.

===Pronunciation===
* {{qualifier|phoneme|standard}}: {{IPA|sl|/t͡ʃ/|[d͡ʒ]}}
* {{qualifier|phoneme|[[wikipedia:Slovene_phonology#t%CA%BC%E2%80%93%C4%8D_distinction|dialects with t’–č distinction]]}}: {{IPA|sl|/t͡ʃ/|/t͡ɕ/|[d͡ʒ]|[d͡ʑ]}}
* {{qualifier|letter name}}: {{IPA|sl|/t͡ʃə́/|/t͡ʃéː/|/t͡ʃèː/}}
* {{qualifier|letter name|linguistics}}: {{sl-IPA|tŕdi čə̏| tŕdi čẹ̄}} ({{l|sl|trdi č}})
* {{rhymes|sl|ə|eː}}

===Letter===
{{sl-letter|upper=Č|lower=č}}

# {{Latn-def|sl|letter|4}}
# {{Latn-def|sl|letter|5|alphabet name=Resian}}
# {{Latn-def|sl|letter|4|alphabet name=Natisone Valley dialect}}

===Symbol===
{{head-lite|sl|symbols|langname=Slovene}}

# {{qualifier|[[wikipedia:Slovene_national_phonetic_transcription|SNPT]]}} ''[[phonetic|Phonetic]] [[transcription]] of sound'' [{{IPAlink|t͡ʃ}}].

===Noun===
{{sl-noun|č|m-in}}

# {{n-g-lite|The name of the [[Appendix:Latin script|Latin script]] letter '''''[[Č]]''''' / '''''[[č]]'''''.}}
# {{lb|sl|linguistics}} {{n-g-lite|The name of the [[phoneme]] ''/{{IPAlink|t͡ʃ}}/''.}}

