Page 743 ć: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From Gaj's Latin alphabet {{m|sh|ć}}, from Polish alphabet {{m|pl|ć}}, from Latin {{m|la|c}}, a modification of uppercase letter {{m|mul|C}}, from Etruscan {{m|ett|𐌂}}, from Ancient Greek {{m|grc|Γ||Gamma}}, from Phoenician {{m|phn|𐤂||gimel}}. Pronunciation as {{IPA|sl|/t͡ʃə/}} is initial Slovene (phoneme plus a fill vowel) and the second pronunciation is probably by analogy of {{der|sl|de|C}} from German.

===Pronunciation===
* {{qualifier|phoneme|standard}}: {{IPA|sl|/t͡ʃ/}}
* {{qualifier|phoneme|dialectal|educated}}: {{IPA|sl|/t͡ɕ/}}
* {{qualifier|letter name|standard}}: {{sl-IPA|méhki čə̏| méhki čẹ̄}} ({{l|sl|mehki č}})
* {{qualifier|letter name|dialectal|educated}}: {{IPA|sl|/t͡ɕə́/|/t͡ɕéː/|/t͡ɕèː/}}
* {{rhymes|sl|ə|eː}}

===Letter===
{{sl-letter|upper=Ć|lower=ć}}

# {{ng|Additional letter used primarily in loanwords from [[Serbo-Croatian]].}}
# {{Latn-def|sl|letter|6|alphabet name=Resian}}

===Symbol===
{{head-lite|sl|symbols|langname=Slovene}}

# {{qualifier|[[wikipedia:Slovene_national_phonetic_transcription|SNPT]]}} ''[[phonetic|Phonetic]] [[transcription]] of sound'' [{{IPAlink|t͡ɕ}}].

===Noun===
{{sl-noun|ć|m-in}}

# {{n-g-lite|The name of the [[Appendix:Latin script|Latin script]] letter '''''[[Ć]]''''' / '''''[[ć]]'''''.}}

====Inflection====
* Overall more common
{{sl-decl-noun-m|ć|ć-j}}

* More common when with a definite adjective
{{sl-decl-noun-table2|ć|ć|ć|ć|ć|ć|ć|ć|ć|ć|ć|ć|ć|ć|ć|ć|ć|ć|title=Masculine inan., no endings}}

===See also===
* {{l|sl|c}}
* {{l|sl|č}}

===References===
{{cite-book|last=Steenwijk|first=Han|title=Ortografia resiana = Tö jošt rozajanskë pïsanjë|publisher=CLEUP|year=1994|location=Padua|worklang=it, sl}}

-------- end text --------
