===Etymology===
From Gaj's Latin alphabet {{m|sh|Ć}}, from Czech alphabet {{m|cs|Č}}, from latin {{m|la|C}}, from Etruscan {{m|ett|𐌂}}, from Ancient Greek {{m|grc|Γ||Gamma}}, from Phoenician {{m|phn|𐤂||gimel}}. Pronunciation as {{IPA|sl|/t͡ʃə/}} is initial Slovene (phoneme plus a fill vowel) and the second pronunciation is probably by analogy of {{der|sl|de|C}} from German.

===Pronunciation===
* {{qualifier|phoneme|standard}}: {{IPA|sl|/t͡ʃ/}}
* {{qualifier|phoneme|dialectal|educated}}: {{IPA|sl|/t͡ɕ/}}
* {{qualifier|letter name|standard}}: {{sl-IPA|méhki čə̏| méhki čẹ̄}} ({{l|sl|mehki č}})
* {{qualifier|letter name|dialectal|educated}}: {{IPA|sl|/t͡ɕə́/|/t͡ɕéː/|/t͡ɕèː/}}
* {{rhymes|sl|ə|eː}}

===Letter===
{{sl-letter|upper=Ć|lower=ć}}

# {{ng|Additional letter used primarily in loanwords from [[Serbo-Croatian]].}}
