Page 964 dva: -------- begin text --------
{{number box|sl|2}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sl|sla-pro|*dъva}}, from {{inh|sl|ine-bsl-pro|*duwō}}, from {{inh|sl|ine-pro|*dwóh₁}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{sl-IPA|dvȃ}}
* {{rhymes|sl|aː}}
* {{hyphenation|sl|dva}}

===Numeral===
{{sl-num|dvȃ}}

# [[two]]
# {{lb|sl|by extension}} a relatively small number
#: {{uxi|sl|Če živiš v mestu imaš '''dva''' koraka do česarkoli.|If you live in a city, everything is only '''a few''' steps away.}}

====Usage notes====
When counting or reciting numbers, the feminine form {{m|sl|dvé}} is formally used.

====Declension====
{{sl-decl-num2|dvȃ|dvẹ̄h|dvẹ̄ma|accm=dvȃ|dvẹ̄h|dvẹ̄ma|dvȃ|dvẹ̑|dvẹ̄h|dvẹ̄ma|dvẹ̑|dvẹ̄h|dvẹ̄ma|dvẹ̑|{{l|sl|dvẹ̑}}, ''{{l|sl|dvȃ}}''|dvẹ̄h|dvẹ̄ma|{{l|sl|dvẹ̑}}, ''{{l|sl|dvȃ}}''|dvẹ̄h|dvẹ̄ma|{{l|sl|dvẹ̑}}, ''{{l|sl|dvȃ}}''|declension type=1|soft?=no|accent=4b|irregtitle=special accent changes{{cln|sl|adjectives with special accent changes}}, irregular genitive and locative endings|n=du
}}
* The neuter nominative/accusative/vocative form ''dvȃ'' is a consequence of common loss of dual of neuter nouns. The form therefore binds with plural forms and is colloquial:
** {{uxi|sl|dve okni|two windows}} (formally)
** {{uxi|sl|dva okna|two windows}} (colloquially)

===Noun===
{{sl-noun|dvȃ|n}}

# {{lb|sl|informal}} number [[two]]
#: {{syn|sl|dve|dvojka}}

====Declension====
{{sl-infl-noun
|||dvȃ||stemtone=c
|gender=n
|declension type=3
|accent=1
|n=sg
|below=To express dual and plural, the phrase ''število dve'' 'number two' is used, e.g. ''dve '''števili dve''' sta napisani'', or, informally, also ''{{l|sl|dvojka}}''.
}}

