===Etymology===
From Gaj's Latin alphabet {{m|sh|Đ}}, from {{der|sl|cs|-}} alphabet {{m|cs|D}}, from Latin {{m|la|D}}, from the {{der|sl|ett|-}} letter {{m|ett|𐌃||de}}, from the {{der|sl|grc|-}} letter {{m|grc|Δ||delta}}, derived from the {{der|sl|phn|-}} letter {{m|phn|𐤃||dalet}}, from an uncertain origin, likely the {{der|sl|egy|-}} hieroglyph {{m|egy|𓉿}}. Pronunciation as {{IPA|sl|/d͡ʒə/}} is initial Slovene (phoneme plus a fill vowel) and the second pronunciation is probably by analogy from {{der|sl|de|D}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{qualifier|phoneme|standard}}: {{IPA|sl|/d͡ʒ/|[t͡ʃ]}}
* {{qualifier|phoneme|dialectal|educated}}: {{IPA|sl|/d͡ʑ/|[t͡ɕ]}}
* {{qualifier|letter name|standard}}: {{sl-IPA|méhki džə̏| méhki džẹ̄}} ({{l|sl|mehki dž}})
* {{qualifier|letter name|educated}}: {{IPA|sl|/d͡ʑə́/|/d͡ʑéː/|/d͡ʑèː/}}
* {{rhymes|sl|ə|eː}}

