Page 1086 f: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=sl}}

===Etymology 1===
From Gaj's Latin alphabet {{m|sh|f}}, from {{der|sl|cs|-}} alphabet {{m|cs|f}}, which is a modification of upper case Latin letter {{m|mul|F}}, from Greek {{der|sl|grc|-}} letter {{m|grc|Ϝ||digamma}}, derived from the {{der|sl|phn|-}} letter {{m|phn|𐤅||waw}}, from the {{der|sl|egy|-}} hieroglyph {{m|egy|𓏲}}. Pronunciation as {{IPA|sl|/fə/}} is initial Slovene (phoneme plus a fill vowel) and the second pronunciation is probably taken from {{der|sl|de|f}}.

====Pronunciation====
* Phoneme
{{sl-pronounce
|IPAt={{IPA|sl|/f/|[v]}}
|SNPTt={{SNPT|/f/|[v]}}
|IPAnt={{IPA|sl|/f/|[v]}}
|SNPTnt={{SNPT|/f/|[v]}}
}}

* Letter name
{{sl-pronounce
|nt=f
|phonetic=fə̀, èf
|tonal=ə̏, ȅ
|IPAt={{IPA|sl|[ˈfə̂]|[ˈɛ̂f]}}
|SNPTt={{SNPT|[fə̏]|[ȅf]}}
|IPAnt={{IPA|sl|[ˈfə]|[ˈɛf]}}
|SNPTnt={{SNPT|[fə̀]|[èf]}}
|audiont={{audio|sl|Sl-nt-f.ogg}}, {{audio|sl|Sl-nt-ef.ogg}}
}}
{{sl-pronounce-other
|rhymes={{rhymes|sl|ə|ɛf}}
|rhymesSNPT=ə̀, èf
|hyphenation={{hyphenation|sl|f}}
|homophonest={{homophones|sl|F|f}}
|homophonesnt={{homophones|sl|F|f}}
