# {{Latn-def|sl|letter|7}}
# {{Latn-def|sl|letter|10|alphabet name=Resian}}
# {{Latn-def|sl|letter|7|alphabet name=Natisone Valley dialect}}

====Symbol====
{{head|sl|symbol}}

# {{qualifier|[[wikipedia:Slovene_national_phonetic_transcription|SNPT]]}} ''[[phonetic|Phonetic]] [[transcription]] of sound'' [{{IPAlink|f}}].

====Noun====
{{sl-noun|f|m-in}}

# {{n-g-lite|The name of the [[Appendix:Latin script|Latin script]] letter '''''[[F]]''''' / '''''[[f]]'''''.}}
# {{lb|sl|linguistics}} {{n-g-lite|The name of the [[phoneme]] ''/{{IPAlink|f}}/''.}}

=====Inflection=====
* First pronunciation
{{sl-decl-noun-table3|f|f-ja|[[f-ju]], ''[[f-ji]]''|f|[[f-ju]], ''[[f-ji]]''|f-jem|f|f-ja|f-jev|f-jema|f-ja|f-jih|f-jema|f-ja|f-ji|f-jev|f-jem|f-je|f-jih|f-ji|f-ji|decl=m-in-1-s|infix=j-}}

* Second pronunciation
{{sl-decl-noun-table3|f|f-a|[[f-u]], ''[[f-i]]''|f|[[f-u]], ''[[f-i]]''|f-om|f|f-a|f-ov|f-oma|f-a|f-ih|f-oma|f-a|f-i|f-ov|f-om|f-e|f-ih|f-i|f-i|decl=m-in-1}}

* More common when with a definite adjective
{{sl-decl-noun-table3|f|f|f|f|f|f|f|f|f|f|f|f|f|f|f|f|f|f|f|f|f|decl=m-3}}

* First pronunciation, dialectal, in common written language used till 19th century
{{sl-decl-noun-table3|f|f-ja|[[f-ju]], ''[[f-ji]]''|f|[[f-ju]], ''[[f-ji]]''|f-jom|f|f-ja|f-jov|f-joma|f-ja|f-jih|f-joma|f-ja|f-ji|f-jov|f-jom|f-je|f-jih|f-ji|f-ji|decl=m-in-1|infix=j-}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{m|en|f}}, an abbreviation for {{m|en|fuck}}, from {{der|sl|enm|*fukken}}, probably from {{der|sl|gem-pro|*fukkōną#Etymology_2}}, from {{der|sl|ine-pro|*pewǵ-|t=to strike, punch, stab}}.

====Pronunciation====
