{{sl-decl-noun-table3|f|f-a|[[f-u]], ''[[f-i]]''|f|[[f-u]], ''[[f-i]]''|f-em|f|f-a|f-ev|f-ema|f-a|f-ih|f-ema|f-a|f-i|f-ev|f-em|f-e|f-ih|f-i|f-i|decl=m-in-1}}

===Etymology 3===
A dialectal variant of {{l|sl|v}} made by analogy to {{l|sl|s}}/{{l|sl|z}} in dialects where [{{IPAlink|w}}] turned into [{{IPAlink|v}}] and got its devoiced part, [{{IPAlink|f}}].

