From {{inh|sl|sla-pro|*glupъ}}. Cognate with {{cog|sh|sc=Cyrl|глу̏пав}}/{{m|sh|glȕpav}}, {{cog|bg|глупав}}, {{cog|ru|глупый}}, {{cog|sk|hlúpy}}. Non-Slavic cognates include Old Norse {{m|non|glópr}}. According to [[:w:de:Erich Berneker|Erich Berneker]] and [[:w:Christianus Cornelius Uhlenbeck|Uhlenbeck]] the Slavic words were borrowed from a {{der|sl|gem}} source, which is contested by [[:w:Max Vasmer|Vasmer]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{sl-IPA|glȗp}}

===Adjective===
{{sl-adj|glȗp|bolj}}

# {{lb|sl|archaic}} [[dumb]], [[stupid]], [[moronic]]

====Inflection====
{{sl-decl-adj|glúp}}

===References===
* {{R:ru:Vasmer|глупый}}
* {{R:sla:SEW|vol=I|page=309}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:sl:Fran}}

