===Etymology===
From {{inh|sl|sla-pro|*gospoďa}}. There was an irregular contraction (*oďa →) *oja → a; the obsolete form {{l|sl|gospoja}} still retains the regular form (compare with earlier contraction {{l|sla-pro|*lìpa|*lìpojǫ}} → {{lang|sla-pro|*lìpǭ}} in instrumental singular a-stem ending).

===Pronunciation===
* {{sl-IPA|gospá}}

===Noun===
{{sl-noun|gospá|f|m=gospọ̑d}}

# [[Mrs]]
# [[lady]]
#: {{syn|sl|dama|ga.|gospoja|madam|madama|šinjora|šjora}}
# {{lb|sl|archaic}} female [[lord]], [[master]]
#: {{syn|sl|gospodarȋca}}
# {{lb|sl|archaic|of|a [[servant]]}} female [[employer]]
# {{lb|sl|rare}} [[wife]]
#: {{syn|sl|žéna}}

