#: {{syn|sl|eh|e|o}}
#: {{ux|sl|'''I''' ja, saj ti verjamem.|'''Whatever''', I believe you.}}

===Etymology 4===
Derived from {{der|sl|sla-pro|*i||and}}, itself from {{inh|sl|ine-pro|*éy}}, an early locative singular determiner, formed from the root {{m|ine-pro|*h₁e-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*h₁o-}}. Cognates with {{cog|sh|i}}, {{cog|mk|и}}, {{cog|bg|и}}, {{cog|cu|и}}, {{cog|cs|i}}, {{cog|pl|i}}, {{cog|csb|ë}}, {{cog|sk|i}}, {{cog|be|і}}, {{cog|be|й}}, {{cog|rue|й}}, {{cog|uk|і}}, {{cog|uk|й}}, and {{cog|ru|и}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{sl-pronounce
|nt=i, ì
|t=ȉ
|IPAt={{IPA|sl|[i]|[ˈî]}}
|SNPTt={{SNPT|[i]|[ȉ]}}
|IPAnt={{IPA|sl|[i]|[ˈi]}}
|SNPTnt={{SNPT|[i]|[ì]}}
}}
{{sl-pronounce-other
|rhymes={{rhymes|sl|i}}
|rhymesSNPT={{SNPTchar|[-ì]}}
|homophonest={{homophones|sl|i}}
|homophonesl={{homophones|sl|i|I}}
|hyphenation={{hyph|sl|i}}
}}

====Conjunction====
{{head|sl|conjunctions}}

# {{lb|sl|obsolete}} [[and]]
#: {{syn|sl|in|ino|no|ter|pa}}

=====Usage notes=====
Use of '''i''' as a conjunction in Slovene is obsolete and not well-known, so most nowadays speakers usually relate it with other Slavic languages rather than with old Slovene. Nowadays, its derivative, {{l|sl|in}} is used, which is etymologically speaking a stressed variant, but has since lost the initial difference.

As opposed to {{l|sl|in}}, '''i''' can be pronounced as stressed or unstressed form in all contexts (but if taken out of context, only the stressed version is allowed) whereas ''in'' is stressed only if taken out of context.

