# {{lb|sl|imperfective}} to [[have]]
#: {{syn|sl|premóči|razpolȃgati|posedováti}}
#* {{quote-journal|sl|author=Valentin Zarnik|title=Originali iz domačega življenja|work=Novice gospodarskih, obertnijskih in narodskih stvarí|page=242|passage=On je bil mož principov in načel, v vsem obnašanju in za vsako zadevo je '''imel''' svoje načelo.|translation=He was a man of principles and [[tenet]]s, for all behavioral traits and every subject he '''had''' his principle.|year=1862|location=Ljubljana|series=20}}
# {{lb|sl|imperfective}} to [[have]] with
#: {{syn|sl|nosīti|vlẹ́či|vlačīti}}
#: {{ux|sl|Vozniško dovoljenje '''imam''' vedno s seboj, tudi če ne vozim|I '''have''' my driving licence always '''with''' me, even if I don't drive.}}
# {{lb|sl|imperfective}} to have in [[stock]], to [[offer]]
#: {{syn|sl|núditi|ponújati}}
#: {{ux|sl|Spomladi '''ima''' vsaka tržnica sveže jagode.|Every market '''offers''' fresh strawberries in the spring.}}
# {{lb|sl|imperfective}} to be [[old]]
#: {{syn|sl|bíti stȁr}}
#: {{uxi|sl|Moja hči '''ima''' že deset let.|My daughter '''is''' already ten years '''old'''.}}
# {{q|imperfective|colloquial}} to [[tempt]]
#: {{syn|sl|mȋkati}}
#: {{uxi|sl|'''Ima''' me, da bi te udaril.|I '''want''' to slap you right now.}}
# {{lb|sl|imperfective}} to [[breed]]
#: {{syn|sl|gojīti|redīti}}
# {{q|imperfective|rare}} to [[find]], to form an [[opinion]]
#: {{syn|sl|držáti|jemáti|smȃtrati|štẹ́ti|traktȋrati}}
#: {{uxi|sl|To trditev '''imam''' za pravilno.|I '''think''' this statement is true.}}
# {{q|imperfective|colloquial}} to wear
#: {{syn|sl|nosīti|imẹ́ti oblẹ̑čeno}}
# {{lb|sl|imperfective}} ''Used to signify [[smug]], similar to the verb '' get what one deserves.
#: {{syn|sl|dobīti, kar kdo išče}}
#: {{ux|sl|Dolgo je najedal, zdaj pa '''ima'''!|He was nagging for a long time, but he '''got what he deserved'''!}}
# {{lb|sl|perfective}} to [[give birth]]
#: {{syn|sl|rodīti|skotīti}}
#* {{quote-web|sl|author=Mojca Lorenčič|title=Starost res ni obdobje, ko bi ženska zanosila in imela otroka|passage=Starost res ni obdobje, ko bi ženska zanosila in '''imela''' otroka|translation=Oldness is really not the time to '''have''' children.|year=2005|url=https://www.dnevnik.si/111309|work=Dnevnik}}
# {{lb|sl|imperfective}} to be rich
#: {{syn|sl|imẹ́ti pod pȃlcem}}
#: {{uxi|sl|On pa '''ima'''.|He '''is rich'''.}}
# {{lb|sl|reflexive}} to [[do]], to perform
#: {{uxi|sl|Lepo se '''imam'''.|I am '''doing''' well.}}
# {{q|imperfective|obsolete}} to [[seize]], to [[capture]]
#: {{uxi|sl|Žeja me '''ima'''.|I '''am''' thirsty.}}
# {{q|modal|obsolete}} [[should]], [[must]]
#: {{syn|sl|mọ̑rati}}
#: {{uxi|sl|'''Imel''' bi pridnejši biti.|You '''should''' be more diligent.}}
# {{q|auxiliary|obsolete|northern Littoral dialects}} Used to form future tense.
#* {{quote-book|sl|title=Celovški rokopis|page=1|passage=Gory yiede w nebeſſa ſeydi kch deſſnuttczy boga otſche wſemogotſchiga od tody kch '''iyma''' priti ſoditi ſywe yno mortwe.|translation=He ascended into heaven, and sits at the right hand of the God, the almighty Father, where he '''will''' come from and judge the living and the dead.|year=around 1380}}

