Page 1656 iti: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
A suppletive paradigm of three verbs:
* The infinitive and supine from {{inh|sl|sla-pro|*jьti}}, from {{inh|sl|ine-pro|*h₁éyti}}. This verb was itself suppletive in Proto-Slavic, with a different stem for the l-participle.
* The future and imperative from a prefixed {{inh|sl|sla-pro|*pojьti}}.
* The present tense from {{inh|sl|sla-pro|*gręsti}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{sl-IPA|īti}}
* {{hyphenation|sl|í|ti}}

===Verb===
{{sl-verb|īti|both}}

# to [[go]]
#: {{ant|sl|príti}}
#: {{uxi|sl|iti v šolo|to go to school}}

====Inflection====
{{sl-infl-iti}}

