===Alternative forms===
* {{l|sl|ſad}} {{q|Bohorič alphabet}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sl|sla-pro|*sȃdъ||plant, garden}}, from {{inh|sl|ine-bsl-pro|*sādas}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{sl-IPA|sȃd}}
* {{rhymes|sl|aːt}}
* {{hyphenation|sl|sad}}
* {{homophones|sl|sat}}

===Noun===
{{sl-noun|sȃd|m-in}}

# {{lb|sl|archaic|or|literary}} [[fruit]]
#: {{syn|sl|sadež|plod}}
# {{lb|sl|literary}} [[result]], [[outcome]]
#: {{syn|sl|rezultat|izraz|odraz|pridobitev|otrok|output|posledica|produkt|plod}}
# {{lb|sl|obsolete}} [[child]], young direct [[offspring]]
#: {{syn|sl|otrok|dete|froc|malček|otroček|otročič|otročiček|otrokec|pamž|pestovanček|pestovanec|spestovanec}}
#: {{ant|sl|starš|roditelj|rodnik|starši}}
#: {{uxi|sl|Zdrava, Marija, milosti polna, Gospod je s Teboj, blagoslovljena si med ženami in blagoslovljen je '''sad''' Tvojega telesa Jezus.|Hail Mary, full of grace, the Lord is with thee. Blessed art thou amongst women, and blessed is the '''fruit''' of thy womb, Jesus.}}
# {{lb|sl|literary|rare}} [[consequence]]
#: {{syn|sl|posledica|nasledek|nastopek|posledek|plod}}

====Usage notes====
Unlike ''{{l|sl|plod}}'', ''sad'' is used more when the edibility is stressed, rather than the seeds it contains.

