Page 5527 đ: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=sl}}

===Etymology 1===
From Gaj's Latin alphabet {{m|sh|đ}}, from Czech alphabet {{m|cs|d}}, from Latin {{m|la|d}}, which is a modification of capital letter {{m|mul|D}}, from {{der|sl|grc|-}} letter {{m|grc|Δ||Delta}}. Pronunciation as {{IPA|sl|/d͡ʑə/}} is initial Slovene (phoneme plus a fill vowel) and the second pronunciation is probably by analogy from {{der|sl|de|d}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{qualifier|phoneme|standard}}: {{IPA|sl|/d͡ʒ/|[t͡ʃ]}}
* {{qualifier|phoneme|dialectal|educated}}: {{IPA|sl|/d͡ʑ/|[t͡ɕ]}}
* {{qualifier|letter name|standard}}: {{sl-IPA|méhki džə̏| méhki džẹ̄}} ({{l|sl|mehki dž}})
* {{qualifier|letter name|educated}}: {{IPA|sl|/d͡ʑə́/|/d͡ʑéː/|/d͡ʑèː/}}
* {{rhymes|sl|ə|eː}}

====Letter====
{{sl-letter|upper=Đ|lower=đ}}

# {{ng|Additional letter used primarily in loanwords from [[Serbo-Croatian]].}}

====Noun====
{{sl-noun|đ|m-in}}

# {{n-g-lite|The name of the [[Appendix:Latin script|Latin script]] letter '''''[[Đ]]''''' / '''''[[đ]]'''''.}}

=====Inflection=====
* Overall more common
{{sl-decl-noun-m|đ|đ-j}}

* More common when with a definite adjective
{{sl-decl-noun-table2|đ|đ|đ|đ|đ|đ|đ|đ|đ|đ|đ|đ|đ|đ|đ|đ|đ|đ|title=Masculine inan., no endings}}

===Etymology 2===
Letter {{l|sl|d}} with a stroke to signify partial spirantization, which is sometimes also used in other phonetic transcriptions.

====Pronunciation====
* {{q|sound|unofficial}}: {{IPA|sl|[d̞]}}

====Symbol====
{{head-lite|sl|symbols|langname=Slovene}}

# {{qualifier|[[wikipedia:Slovene_national_phonetic_transcription|SNPT]]}} ''[[phonetic|Phonetic]] [[transcription]] of sound'' [{{IPAlink|d̞|d}}].

=====Usage notes=====
Although by the description, the corresponding IPA representation should be approximately [{{IPAlink|d̞|d}}], no equivalent IPA representation is given in the source.

===See also===
* {{l|sl|d}}

===References===
* {{cite-book|sl|last=Kenda-Jež |first=Karmen |date=February 27, 2017 |title=Fonetična trankripcija |trans-title=Phonetic transcription |url=https://fran.si/150/sla-slovenski-lingvisticni-atlas-1/datoteke/SLA1_Foneticna-transkripcija.pdf |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220122221458/https://www.fran.si/150/sla-slovenski-lingvisticni-atlas-1/datoteke/SLA1_Foneticna-transkripcija.pdf |archivedate=January 22, 2022 |accessdate=March 19, 2022 |publisher=Znanstvenoraziskovalni center [[SAZU]], Inštitut za slovenski jezik Frana Ramovša |pages=27–30 }}

-------- end text --------
Page 5528 ė: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Letter {{l|sl|e}} with dot above ({{l|sl|̇|◌̇}}) to signify a lot more close vowel.

====Pronunciation====
* {{qualifier|sound|unofficial}}: {{IPA|sl|[ɪ͈]}}

====Symbol====
{{head-lite|sl|symbols|langname=Slovene}}

# {{qualifier|[[wikipedia:Slovene_national_phonetic_transcription|dialectal transcription]]}} ''[[phonetic|Phonetic]] [[transcription]] of tense sound between '' [{{IPAlink|e}}] ''and'' [{{IPAlink|i}}].

=====Usage notes=====
Although by the description, the corresponding IPA representation should be approximately [{{IPAlink|ɪ͈|ɪ}}], no equivalent IPA representation is given in the source.

===Etymology 2===
Letter {{l|sl|e}} with dot above ({{l|sl|̇|◌̇}}) to signify an extra short vowel.

